{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5d9a41b7-3c62-4f08-9a1e-7c6b2d4e8f31",
    "name": "OPS File Handler API (v1)",
    "description": "Everything the File Handler Portal can do, callable from another application: search or import a booking, maintain flights and hotels, fix contacts, raise a cancellation, and generate or email the Booking Update PDF.\n\n**Start here:** select the \"File Handler API — OPS Live\" environment, put a real approved file handler's portal login into {{fh_credential}} / {{fh_password}}, then run `Auth → 1. Login` (the token is stored automatically into {{access_token}}).\n\nBookings are addressed by **booking ref**, **IS number** or **CNTL number** — whichever you have. Requests are ordered so the folders can be run top to bottom: Flights and Accommodations capture the ids they create into {{flight_id}} / {{acc_id}} for the update and delete calls that follow.\n\nFull reference: FileHandler-API.md",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Applies to every request in the collection.",
          "// The PDF download returns a binary body, so only assert the envelope on JSON.",
          "const type = pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type') || '';",
          "if (type.includes('application/json')) {",
          "    pm.test('Response is JSON with the standard envelope', function () {",
          "        const body = pm.response.json();",
          "        pm.expect(body).to.have.property('success');",
          "        pm.expect(body).to.have.property('request_id');",
          "        pm.expect(body).to.have.property('timestamp');",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "https://ops.aahaas.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "api_base", "value": "{{base_url}}/api/public/fh/v1", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "0. Discover the API (no token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "console.log(d.name + ' v' + d.version + ' — ' + d.endpoints.length + ' endpoints');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{api_base}}", "host": ["{{api_base}}"] },
            "description": "Service discovery and health check. Lists every endpoint and the scope it needs, straight from the running server. No token required."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1. Login (file handler)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Token returned', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.token_type).to.eql('Bearer');",
                  "});",
                  "// Store the token for every other request in the collection.",
                  "pm.environment.set('access_token', body.data.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('token_expires_at', body.data.expires_at);",
                  "if (body.data.file_handler) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('file_handler_id', body.data.file_handler.id);",
                  "}",
                  "console.log('Token stored — valid until ' + body.data.expires_at);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"credential\": \"{{fh_credential}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{fh_password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{api_base}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{api_base}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Logs in with a real file handler's portal credentials — email or phone, plus password. The token carries scope `*`, so it can do everything the portal can, and every action is attributed to that handler.\n\nThe test script saves the token into {{access_token}}."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Login (service client, acts for a handler)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Service token', () => pm.expect(body.data.subject_type).to.eql('service'));",
                  "// Uncomment to run the rest of the collection as the service client:",
                  "// pm.environment.set('access_token', body.data.access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{fh_service_username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{fh_service_password}}\",\n  \"act_as\": \"{{act_as}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{api_base}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{api_base}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "For a machine account configured with FH_PUBLIC_API_USERNAME / FH_PUBLIC_API_PASSWORD, so the calling app never stores handler passwords.\n\n`act_as` names the file handler every write is attributed to; it can also be sent per request as the `X-File-Handler` header. Without either (and without a server default) calls fail with 400 ACT_AS_REQUIRED."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Verify token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Token valid', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.valid).to.be.true);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{api_base}}/auth/verify", "host": ["{{api_base}}"], "path": ["auth", "verify"] },
            "description": "Cheap probe — call it before a batch run instead of discovering an expired token halfway through a flight upload."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Who am I",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "console.log(d.file_handler.name + ' — ' + d.stats.bookings_touched + ' bookings touched');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{api_base}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{api_base}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] },
            "description": "Profile of the file handler this token acts as, plus how many actions and bookings they have to their name."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Is this email registered? (no token)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/auth/register?email={{fh_credential}}",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"],
              "query": [{ "key": "email", "value": "{{fh_credential}}" }]
            },
            "description": "Live availability check for a sign-up form. Returns nothing but `exists` and `approved`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Register a new file handler (no token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// 201 first time, 409 ALREADY_REGISTERED afterwards — both are correct.",
                  "pm.test('201 Created or 409 already registered', () => pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Test Handler\",\n  \"email\": \"test.handler@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"ChangeMe123\",\n  \"phone\": \"+94 77 123 4567\",\n  \"whatsapp_phone\": \"+94 77 123 4567\",\n  \"country\": \"SRILANKA\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{api_base}}/auth/register", "host": ["{{api_base}}"], "path": ["auth", "register"] },
            "description": "Creates a **pending** account. An ultra/super admin must approve it in /dashboard/admin/file-handlers before it can log in.\n\nDo not run this against the live server unless a real handler is being onboarded."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Bookings",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Search by ref / IS / CNTL",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "console.log(d.count + ' result(s) for ' + d.query);",
                  "if (d.count) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('booking_ref', d.results[0].booking_ref);",
                  "    const f = d.results[0].flights[0];  if (f) pm.environment.set('flight_id', f.id);",
                  "    const a = d.results[0].accommodations[0];  if (a) pm.environment.set('acc_id', a.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/search?q={{booking_ref}}&limit=10",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "search"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "q", "value": "{{booking_ref}}" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "10" },
                { "key": "auto_import", "value": "true", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "The portal's search box. Space-insensitive: \"IS 40475\" and \"IS40475\" find the same booking. Each hit comes back complete — flights, hotels, passengers, contacts, cancellation trail.\n\nEnable `auto_import=true` to have a miss pulled in from AppleSystem instead of returning an empty list (needs the booking:import scope)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get one booking",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json().data.booking;",
                  "console.log(b.booking_ref + ' → ' + b.status + ' · ' + b.flights.length + ' flights · ' + b.accommodations.length + ' hotels');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}"]
            },
            "description": "Everything the file handler sees for one booking. `{ref}` may be the booking ref, the IS number or the CNTL number."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Import from AppleSystem",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created or 200 already exists', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "if (d) console.log(d.booking.booking_ref + ' — already_existed=' + d.already_existed);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"q\": \"{{booking_ref}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/import", "host": ["{{api_base}}"], "path": ["bookings", "import"] },
            "description": "For a booking that exists as a confirmed AppleSystem quotation but was never imported into OPS. Idempotent — a booking that already exists comes back with `already_existed: true`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update contacts + important notes",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "console.log('changed: ' + JSON.stringify(pm.response.json().data.changed_fields));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"agent_email\": \"ops@makemytrip.com\",\n  \"agent_phone\": \"+91 22 1234 5678\",\n  \"agent_whatsapp\": \"+91 98765 43210\",\n  \"contact_email\": \"guest@example.com\",\n  \"contact_phone\": \"+91 98111 22333\",\n  \"contact_whatsapp\": \"+91 98111 22333\",\n  \"important_notes\": \"Vegetarian meals throughout. Guest lands with a wheelchair request.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}"]
            },
            "description": "The only booking fields a file handler may edit. Send just the ones that changed; send \"\" to clear one. PUT behaves identically.\n\nStatus, pax, dates and prices are deliberately not editable here."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Flights",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List flights",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "if (d.count) pm.environment.set('flight_id', d.flights[0].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/flights",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "flights"]
            },
            "description": "Every flight on the booking, earliest first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add one flight",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.environment.set('flight_id', d.flights[0].id);",
                  "console.log('flight_id stored: ' + d.flights[0].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"flight_no\": \"UL309\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-09-04\",\n  \"from_airport\": \"BOM\",\n  \"dep_time\": \"01:25\",\n  \"to_airport\": \"CMB\",\n  \"arr_time\": \"03:05\",\n  \"airline\": \"SriLankan Airlines\",\n  \"notes\": \"Guest requested aisle seats\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/flights",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "flights"]
            },
            "description": "Required: flight_no, date, from_airport, to_airport. Optional: dep_time, arr_time, airline, notes.\n\ncamelCase spellings (flightNo, fromApt, depTime …) are accepted too, so the output of /flights/extract can be posted back verbatim."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add a whole itinerary (batch)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "console.log('added: ' + pm.response.json().data.added);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"flights\": [\n    {\n      \"flight_no\": \"UL309\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-09-04\",\n      \"from_airport\": \"BOM\",\n      \"dep_time\": \"01:25\",\n      \"to_airport\": \"CMB\",\n      \"arr_time\": \"03:05\",\n      \"airline\": \"SriLankan Airlines\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flight_no\": \"UL308\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-09-11\",\n      \"from_airport\": \"CMB\",\n      \"dep_time\": \"20:40\",\n      \"to_airport\": \"BOM\",\n      \"arr_time\": \"22:35\",\n      \"airline\": \"SriLankan Airlines\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/flights",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "flights"]
            },
            "description": "The batch is validated in full before anything is written, so one bad segment rejects the request rather than leaving half an itinerary in the booking."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Replace a flight",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"flight_no\": \"UL309\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-09-04\",\n  \"from_airport\": \"BOM\",\n  \"dep_time\": \"02:10\",\n  \"to_airport\": \"CMB\",\n  \"arr_time\": \"03:50\",\n  \"airline\": \"SriLankan Airlines\",\n  \"notes\": \"Retimed by the airline\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/flights/{{flight_id}}",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "flights", "{{flight_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "A full replace, not a partial patch — the same required fields as POST apply. PATCH is accepted as an alias."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Extract flights from a ticket (pasted text)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "console.log('extracted ' + d.count + ' segment(s), saved=' + d.saved);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"text\": \"UL 309 04SEP BOM CMB 0125 0305 CONFIRMED\\nUL 308 11SEP CMB BOM 2040 2235 CONFIRMED\",\n  \"save\": false\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/flights/extract",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "flights", "extract"]
            },
            "description": "GPT-4o reads the segments out of pasted e-ticket text. Nothing is written — the parsed flights come back for a human to confirm, then POST them to /flights.\n\nSet \"save\": true to extract and persist in one call."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Extract flights from a ticket (file upload)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                { "key": "file", "type": "file", "src": [], "description": "JPG, PNG, WebP, GIF or PDF — max 10 MB" },
                { "key": "save", "value": "false", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/flights/extract",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "flights", "extract"]
            },
            "description": "The same upload the portal sends. Attach a ticket image or PDF to the `file` field before running.\n\nIf your client cannot do multipart, send JSON instead: { \"file_base64\": \"…\", \"file_name\": \"ticket.pdf\" }."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Remove a flight",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/flights/{{flight_id}}",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "flights", "{{flight_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Removes the flight from the booking. 404 FLIGHT_NOT_FOUND if it is not on that booking."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Accommodations",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List hotels",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "if (d.count) pm.environment.set('acc_id', d.accommodations[0].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/accommodations",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "accommodations"]
            },
            "description": "Every hotel on the booking, earliest check-in first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add a hotel",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.environment.set('acc_id', d.accommodations[0].id);",
                  "console.log('acc_id stored: ' + d.accommodations[0].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"city\": \"Kandy\",\n  \"hotel\": \"Earl's Regency\",\n  \"check_in\": \"2026-09-06\",\n  \"check_out\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"room_type\": \"Deluxe Double\",\n  \"meal_type\": \"HB\",\n  \"address\": \"Tennekumbura, Kandy 20000\",\n  \"contact\": \"+94 81 242 2122\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/accommodations",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "accommodations"]
            },
            "description": "Required: city, hotel, check_in, check_out. `nights` is computed from the dates unless you send it explicitly.\n\nSend { \"accommodations\": [ … ] } to add several at once."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Replace a hotel",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"city\": \"Kandy\",\n  \"hotel\": \"Earl's Regency\",\n  \"check_in\": \"2026-09-06\",\n  \"check_out\": \"2026-09-09\",\n  \"room_type\": \"Executive Suite\",\n  \"meal_type\": \"FB\",\n  \"address\": \"Tennekumbura, Kandy 20000\",\n  \"contact\": \"+94 81 242 2122\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base}}/bookings/{{booking_ref}}/accommodations/{{acc_id}}",
              "host": ["{{api_base}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{booking_ref}}", "accommodations", "{{acc_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "A full replace — the same required fields as POST. PATCH is accepted as an alias. `nights` is recomputed from the new dates."
          }
        },
